<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Price Revolution</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">16th–17th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Price Revolution was a period of sustained <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inflation">inflation</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> during the sixteenth and early seventeenth centuries. It was driven in part by the influx of American <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> flowing through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> to the bankers who financed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> campaigns. The inflation damaged Spanish agriculture and manufacturing, weakening the economic base of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a>.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The flood of silver passed through Spain into European financial systems, above all through repayments to the Genoese and German bankers who financed Habsburg campaigns, and contributed to the <b>Price Revolution</b>, a sustained sixteenth-century inflation that damaged Spanish agriculture and manufacturing relative to northern European competitors.</blockquote><a href="/empire/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire · Socioeconomy</a></li></ul></section>
